      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LEG GODT (1) is the one to beat after winning convincingly at Leinster by nearly two lengths in a Mdn, defeating Inspirational Mac. She's third-up, has placed at about 1400m, and Ebony Johnson's 3kg claim offsets the 60kg, giving her a strong winning profile. DONATALLY (2) is less reliable, with no placings from eight starts, but the Geraldton Mdn was better than it appeared as he started slowly and rallied late. The 1400m remains a question mark. BUON AMICI (4) drops from a Class 2 at Kalgoorlie and eases from provincial races, giving him a chance to improve from a last-start sixth. His best distance form outshines most here. TINY CHAMPION (3) offers consistency, with recent thirds at Leinster and Leonora, and three placings from three attempts at around 1400m make her a legitimate minor hope if she can find that extra length. GIGI GOGO (5) has claims.",
